~ start
do start_talking()
do disable_movement()
Jory: Oh — hey. Boat, was it? Nobody comes by boat any more.
Jory: Welcome to Hearth Hollow, friend. Old fishing town, mostly abandoned. What brings you here?
Traveller: Just heading through.
Jory: You can't, I'm afraid. The road over the ridge was barricaded years back.
Traveller: But I have to.
Jory: Ha. Everyone says that. [wait=0.6] Go and see the Blacksmith, the big house past the meadow. Follow the hammer.
Jory: He's an odd one, but if anyone can get you through, it's him. Have a look around while you're at it — the north shore, the woods.
do stop_talking()
do enable_movement()
=> END

~ again
do start_talking()
Jory: [[Blacksmith's up past the meadow. Follow the hammer.|Road's still blocked, friend. Still.|Have a wander. The hut on the north shore's worth a look.|I'd offer you a tune, but you look like a man with somewhere to be.]]
do stop_talking()
=> END
